begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $L$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $L$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P:$\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37601" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${M}^{16},$ where\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2975c4f9-6dee-5125-bb13-6ec3dea74ab8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323922 #edb/ref 1074 "We have been given the following diagonalization of $M.$\n\n$$\nM={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $M=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${M}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{M}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{16} & =P{D}^{16}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[8]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[4]{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{16}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt[8]{2})^{16} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[4]{2})^{16}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 48 \\\\ 4 & 32\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-32 & 72 \\\\ -24 & 52\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351673 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}19 & -12 \\\\ 32 & -21\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351673 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351673 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ce48fd3-6d90-5867-bc8c-48f781a9a134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352535 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -12 \\\\ 32 & -2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352535 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352535 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6dea34ce-51cc-54ce-bd9e-2e2c5ec68b40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352561 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}19 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -21\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352561 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352561 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71ac80d5-5537-5ad5-953b-dc791c6b3dbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352567 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}19 & -12 \\\\ 21 & -32\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352567 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352567 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7239e333-3699-5e0e-a679-3638ec2f4a51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352637 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -19 \\\\ 32 & -21\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352637